The One True AWK (the awk of Brian Kernighan, second edition), taken
from contrib/one-true-awk of the FreeBSD source tree on the GitHub
mirror https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-src at commit
2e33355ee2bfa0b6d7b61aeca66d9b2b2b7b9e56
on 2026-09-06 with tools/fetch_sedawk.sh. The upstream repository is
https://github.com/onetrue-awk/awk; main.c reports the release date as
its version.

Copied without modification:
  src/   awk.h, awkgram.y, b.c, lex.c, lib.c, main.c, maketab.c, parse.c,
         proto.h, run.c, tran.c, awk.1
  LICENSE, README.md, FIXES

awkgram.y is turned into awkgram.tab.c and awkgram.tab.h by yacc at
build time, and maketab.c, compiled with the host compiler, produces
proctab.c from the grammar's token numbers; the generated files live in
build/user/awk/gen/. user/Makefile links /bin/awk. The vendored files
are exempt from the minios line count and naming conventions. See
docs/design/sedawk.md.
